    STUDY II'S COLLAPSE IS REAL AND ITS MAGNITUDE IS NOT.
    CONTEXT does merge across prefixes on the exact substrate --
    0.2310 is 4.6x chance -- so the mechanism stands.
    The sampler inflates it by 2.0x in this protocol.

    WHAT THIS DOES *NOT* LICENSE. My sparse arm reads
    0.4579, not the published 0.7566, so this is not that
    number re-measured and 0.7566 must NOT be replaced by
    0.2310. Different harness: study II's figure came from the
    next-token training path in PREREG_context_recurrence_off,
    not from create_training_sentences. What transfers is the
    RATIO (2.0x) and the direction; re-deriving 0.7566
    itself needs that harness run on both engines.

    The mechanism is visible in the counts: exact recruits about
    twice the distinct CONTEXT neurons at every prefix length
    (244 vs 108 at length 1, 499 vs 141 at length 2 as measured).
    The sampler confines CONTEXT to a smaller pool, and a smaller
    pool is what makes successive prefixes land on each other.
